@startuml aws-deployment
' ============================================================================
' agentd platform — AWS deployment topology (COMPLETE target; 2026-07-18)
' Boxes are labeled with the real AWS service («type») + its role. Colour = the
' PHASE it is built in (see legend), so this doubles as the build order. No AWS
' sprite icons: the bundled plantuml.jar has no offline icon lib and the online
' sprite URLs are version-fragile — names keep this diagram rendering forever.
' PUML only; do not render PNG unless asked.
' ============================================================================
title agentd platform on AWS — what runs where, why, and in which phase

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam TitleFontSize 17
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #888888
  BackgroundColor #FCFCFC
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBE6
  BorderColor #C8B900
}

' ---- clients (NOT on AWS) --------------------------------------------------
actor "Desktop app / exe user\n(engine on THEIR machine)" as DESK
actor "Browser user\n(engine on OUR fleet)" as WEB
actor "Creator\n(publishes an agent)" as PUB

' ---- edge -------------------------------------------------------------------
package "EDGE (entry into AWS)" as EDGE {
  rectangle "**Route 53**\n<<DNS>>\napp.domain + *.agents.domain\n(per-agent vanity URLs)" as R53 #EAF3FF
  rectangle "**CloudFront**\n<<CDN / TLS>>\nHTTPS + WebSocket proxy;\nforwards viewer Host header" as CF #EAF3FF
  rectangle "**Application Load Balancer**\n<<ALB>>\nWS-aware; spreads users across\nthe engine fleet, sticky per conn" as ALB #EAF3FF
}

' ---- identity ---------------------------------------------------------------
package "IDENTITY" as IDENT {
  rectangle "**Amazon Cognito**\n<<managed auth>>\nsign-in for users + creators;\nissues the ACCOUNT TOKEN" as COG #F0FFF0
}

' ---- compute plane (cattle — runs the image, holds NO durable data) --------
package "COMPUTE plane  (disposable — kill/replace/scale freely)" as COMPUTE {
  rectangle "**Amazon ECR**\n<<image registry>>\nengine image · gateway image ·\nsandbox-runner image" as ECR #F0FFF0
  rectangle "**Model Gateway**\n<<ECS Fargate service>>\nLiteLLM proxy: holds OUR keys,\nmeters per account, enforces plan.\nServes desktop AND web. BYOK skips it." as GW #F0FFF0
  rectangle "**Platform / Registry API**\n<<ECS Fargate service>>\nsign-in glue, publish, entitlements,\nagent provisioning" as API #F0FFF0
  rectangle "**Hosted Runtime — engine fleet**\n<<ECS Fargate service>>\nthe agentd image, multi-user;\nper-connection user_id -> that user's state" as FLEET #EAF3FF
  rectangle "**Sandbox runner**\n<<ECS Fargate task, on-demand>>\nruns an agent's CUSTOM plugin code\nin isolation; mounts only that user's\nagent dir; dies after the run" as SBX #FFF0F0
}

' ---- state plane (crown jewels — durable, isolated, backed up) --------------
package "STATE plane  (durable — the ONLY place user data lives)" as STATE {
  database "**Amazon RDS (PostgreSQL)**\n<<database>>\naccounts · subscriptions ·\nmarketplace listings · entitlements ·\nusage / metering rows" as RDS #FFF0F0
  database "**Amazon EFS**\n<<shared filesystem>>\nper-user state roots:\n/users/<uid>/agents · sessions · memory\n(mounted by the engine fleet)" as EFS #FFF0F0
  database "**Amazon S3**\n<<object store>>\n.agentpkg blobs · uploaded files ·\nbuilt .exe installers" as S3 #FFF0F0
  rectangle "**AWS Secrets Manager**\n<<secrets>>\nOUR provider API keys —\nreadable ONLY by the Model Gateway" as SEC #FFF0F0
}

' ---- distribution + external ------------------------------------------------
rectangle "**Marketplace Registry**\n= Registry API + S3 + RDS\n(the listing IS the share link)" as MKT #F5F0FF
rectangle "LLM / VLM providers\n(Anthropic, Google, ...) — we RENT" as LLM #FCFCFC
rectangle "**CloudWatch**\n<<logs / metrics / alarms>>" as CW #EFEFEF

' ---- flows: why + how -------------------------------------------------------
' desktop: engine is local; ONLY identity + models touch AWS; DATA STAYS LOCAL
DESK --> COG : sign in\n(account token)
DESK --> GW : model calls + token\n(subscription) — or direct\nto provider (BYOK)

' browser: engine runs on our fleet
WEB --> R53 : open agent URL
R53 --> CF
CF --> ALB
ALB --> FLEET : wss
FLEET ..> COG : validate token -> user_id
FLEET --> EFS : read agent + history, write back
FLEET --> S3 : pull .agentpkg / files on demand
FLEET --> GW : model calls (always via gateway)
FLEET --> SBX : dispatch custom-plugin exec
SBX --> EFS : mount ONLY this user's agent dir

' model gateway internals
GW ..> SEC : read provider keys
GW --> RDS : write usage / check plan
GW --> LLM : forward with our key

' image pulls
ECR ..> GW
ECR ..> FLEET
ECR ..> SBX

' publish + marketplace
PUB --> API : publish agent folder
API --> S3 : store .agentpkg + built exe
API --> RDS : listing + entitlement rows
MKT ..> S3
MKT ..> RDS

' ops
FLEET ..> CW
GW ..> CW

legend right
  == Build phase (colour) ==
  <back:#F0FFF0>  Phase 1</back>  Platform Server: Cognito, Model Gateway,
      Registry API, RDS, S3, Secrets, ECR — serves DESKTOP first
  <back:#EAF3FF>  Phase 2</back>  Hosted Runtime: engine fleet, EFS,
      ALB, CloudFront, Route 53 — browser users
  <back:#FFF0F0>  Phase 4</back>  Sandbox runner — unlocks CUSTOM-plugin
      agents on the web (desktop runs them day one)
endlegend

note bottom of STATE
  RULE #5: nothing in the COMPUTE plane stores user data. A Fargate task can die
  and be replaced with zero loss because everything durable lives HERE. Desktop
  is the extreme case: the user's own machine is their state plane (data never
  reaches AWS at all — only identity + model calls do).
end note
@enduml
